WEBVTT

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:17.120
Don't bring back

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:20.450
the terror!

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.320
The terror...

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.170
The United States has determined
that the massive explosion

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:34.540
observed in the Belgistan Republic
by its military satellites

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:38.040
was caused by a weapon of mass
destruction now in development.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:42.240
The US harshly criticized Belgistan
for this development

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:45.310
and in response has decided to
mobilize the Rapid Deployment Force.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:49.250
There is no doubt this is an imperialist
conspiracy prepared for the purposes

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:51.350
of robbing Belgistan of its sovereignty!

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.660
In emergency session, the
UN Security Council,

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:56.190
assembled at the request of
the US Secretary of State,

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:59.260
has adopted a resolution for an
economic embargo of Belgistan.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:03.470
This nation will never fall
prey to such treachery!

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.830
Colonel Stilbanov of the Belgistan
Republic has refused
America has requested deployment
of a multinational force.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:09.240
to allow an inspection by a team from
the Nonproliferation Treaty.
America has requested deployment
of a multinational force.

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:13.240
As of 4 PM, the United Nations has
authorized a multinational NATO force

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:14.810
to be deployed in the region.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.850
The United Nations Security Council
has issued an ultimatum to Belgistan

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:22.680
concerning the acceptance of
inspectors a deadline of 8 PM today.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.950
If we receive no reply by this deadline,
be assured that the UN

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:30.290
will act decisively within ten hours
following the ultimatum's expiration.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.130
Answering questions from
reporters after this,

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:33.700
NATO's General Krause stated that
he was certain, any action,

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.460
should it be taken, will have a decisive
impact within eighteen...

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:40.270
It is believed that behind this rapid
reaction is concern over the support

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:44.270
Belgistan's neighbors are providing.

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:47.810
If military action is at all delayed,
neighboring nations may intervene,

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.180
and this dispute may expand to
become a regional conflict.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:52.110
This shows the transitional pattern of
energy readings taken during contact.
and this dispute may expand to
become a regional conflict.

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:53.680
and this dispute may expand to
become a regional conflict.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:57.750
According to this, if Yushiro
had continued to dance,

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:01.240
the probability of reaching the
final stage was over 90%.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:04.890
It's hard to believe this,

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:06.590
but there was enough there to match
the output of a power plant!

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.200
We were almost there.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:16.340
In any case, you're certain that Yushiro
stopped the experiment on his own?

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:18.200
Yeah, there's no question about that.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:23.240
Today before daylight,

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:25.810
a multinational force of aircraft,
primarily German fighters,

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:29.080
took off from Turkey, and
headed for Belgistan.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:33.350
This is footage from the guidance
system of a Tornado fighter

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:36.360
targeting a radar facility
within Belgistan.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:39.390
How has Yushiro been since?

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:41.830
He won't say anything.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:44.700
That's something that worries me.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:49.570
There is this reoccurring pattern that
comes up in Yushiro's brainwaves.

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:52.540
The only explanation that makes sense
is that he was reacting to something.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:54.610
Something external to him.

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.540
External?

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:00.450
At first I also thought that Yushiro
stopped dancing on his own,

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:02.220
but looking at this...

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:05.710
Are you saying someone interfered
with our experiments from outside?

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:10.860
Today before daybreak, NATO
aircraft originating from Turkey

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:12.730
conducted an aerial bombardment
of Belgistan's capital, Kaha.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:14.760
It's been reported that they were
able to inflict heavy damage

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.600
on several military targets and the
presidential residence.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:20.600
Today before daybreak, multinational
land forces crossed Belgistan's border.

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.570
It appears that a ground war
is now in progress.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:25.470
Today at 4 AM, following an
aerial bombardment,

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:31.250
multinational land forces built around
American, German, and French RDFs,

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:36.780
crossed into Belgistan, and initiated
offensive operations on two fronts.

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:41.120
Over 60% of Belgistan's
military facilities

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:44.460
were neutralized by the air campaign.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:46.860
The typical misinformation campaign.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:59.470
The multinational force inside
Belgistan was met with hostile action.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:03.310
They have smashed through elite
forces, primarily paratroopers,

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:06.780
and have advanced to a point thirty
kilometers from the border.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:07.870
Kiyoharu...

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.750
I somehow managed to get it.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:11.650
So...

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:13.820
An emergency press release
was just made.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:16.620
Multinational forces inside
Belgistan territory

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:20.090
today stormed the capital Kaha, only
to suffer devastating casualties

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:22.290
inflicted by the Belgistan forces, and
have been effectively neutralized.

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:26.570
Finally the official release.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:27.900
This has not been confirmed yet,

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:30.570
but it appears that all units storming
Kaha suffered devastating losses,

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:34.010
and subsequent offensives were
also repelled effectively.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:39.780
This is footage taken from an attack
helicopter escorting the tank column.

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:40.810
Watch closely.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:45.490
What's that?

00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:49.520
LOSAT, a high-speed armor
piercing guided missile.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:53.630
A new missile system that punches
through a tank's hull at high velocity.

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:57.360
I thought even the Americans hadn't
succeeded in developing that yet.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.600
What's a weapon like that doing here?

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:04.040
Actually, the real issue here
is something else.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.610
Almost all the vehicles

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:10.040
were hit and disabled from close range
right after they entered the city.

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:13.950
And many of these attacks
came from building tops,

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.420
as if conducted by infantrymen.

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:17.880
TA's?

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:25.430
This is where the footage ends.

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:27.500
It was shot down.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.760
The most up-to-date attack
helicopter was shot down

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:31.700
by a third rate nation's military.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:40.980
Luckily, the footage survived thanks to
a data link feed going back to the rear.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:42.880
What's Yushiro's condition?

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:45.350
Yushiro is doing fine.

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:48.180
Physiologically, he's almost
completely back to normal.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:50.520
He won't be able to dance yet,

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:53.150
but I think he could handle
a TA operation just fine.

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:04.620
Miss...

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:09.470
I believe you are forbidden
to enter here.

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:12.960
What could be wrong with a
sister visiting her brother?

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:17.170
Please leave us alone for a short time.

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:27.310
Big brother, it's me.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:31.530
I have something I must ask you.

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:37.490
I'm sorry, but please allow me to enter.

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:42.090
Big brother...

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:44.440
Why?

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:47.240
Why are father and my other
brothers doing this?

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:48.610
Why?

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:51.780
What happened that day?
On the stage?

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:58.290
I was not allowed to leave the dressing
room, so I could not watch you dance,

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:01.190
but I felt something unusual
was happening.

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:06.130
No one tells me anything.

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:07.490
Not even Master Sorachi.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:13.840
Kazukiyo says I should not come here.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:15.030
Mother says...

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:18.610
All of this...

00:09:18.610 --> 00:09:20.640
It's as if some experiment is going on!

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:23.710
It's as if they're doing some
experiment with you in it!

00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:25.050
Why?

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:27.820
Why do they treat you like this?

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:31.120
And everyone acts so strange
to only you, big brother!

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:33.490
Why?! I don't know.

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:36.920
Why? Why do you have to be
sent to work with the SSDF,

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:40.360
and dance a Noh that's
like an experiment?

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:47.160
Even when you come back, no one
says anything kind to you.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:50.910
What's wrong with me?

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:54.640
You alone are enduring this treatment.

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:57.480
I couldn't hold back my sadness.

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:01.710
Something...

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:05.510
We were calling out for
something to come.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:10.060
I wonder what it was?

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:11.550
Don't bring back

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:14.430
the terror!

00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:16.860
The terror?

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:22.390
You must not keep it all to
yourself, big brother!

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:28.430
What are you doing here?

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:32.880
I was only...

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:36.720
I thought it had been made clear to
you that you should not come here.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:39.520
Mr. Yushiro is tired.

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:41.010
Come on!

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:58.940
We will experiment using the
temporary facility originally built

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:01.340
for the training of special forces

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:03.830
used in the recent US-Japan joint
training operation, Dimension 05.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:20.930
Having effectively lost the ground war,

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:22.930
the multinational forces have
intensified their air campaign,

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:27.500
provoking criticism from
neighboring nations.

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:31.400
Acts of brutality such as these
will not defeat us!

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:55.100
Tactical Armor, or TA, was developed
in conjunction with the SSDF.

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:59.130
As you can see, it is a multipurpose
land engagement weapons platform

00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:01.600
that employs bipedal movement.

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:05.340
This allows for a drastically wider
range of maneuverability

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:08.280
compared to current forms of
ground movement,

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:14.420
granting it the ability to move about in
almost any form of imaginable terrain.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:18.850
But the unstable nature of this form of
movement makes control very difficult,

00:12:18.850 --> 00:12:22.820
leading many to believe its realization
would be extraordinarily difficult.

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:28.100
Since so many factors come into play
in movement over complex terrain,

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:32.100
at this time, generally speaking,
it would be virtually impossible

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:37.470
to construct a system to be able to
do so with current DSP technology.

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:39.640
Are you saying that neither
the Germans

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:42.210
nor the Americans have come
up with this then?

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:43.680
That's correct.

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:46.480
And we have succeeded
in developing it?

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:49.950
You might call it a victory made
possible by reposing the question.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:54.820
Instead of a central control
mechanism in charge of transmission,

00:12:54.820 --> 00:12:57.860
we embedded control inside the
transmission system itself.

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:04.500
Over 98% of movement control is
carried out in the transmission system.

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:09.000
Is that similar to the autonomous
nervous system seen in nature?

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.870
Something similar to that, yes.

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:13.940
If you look at the movement
of creatures in nature,

00:13:13.940 --> 00:13:16.080
normal body posture is controlled
not by the brain

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:19.880
but by the nervous system localized
in the spinal cord and such.

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:24.950
Furthermore, their agility improves
with experience.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:30.050
Please assume the same applies to the
control system in the TA as well.

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:37.160
In some ways, it can be argued that
the TA's system is more advanced.

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:41.940
In practical terms, let's say you want
to move to a point in front of you.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:47.680
The pilot only has to designate the
destination point, and advance.

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:52.450
The transmission will evaluate which
pattern of movement will be the best,

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:57.150
while keeping in mind the personality
and physical attributes of the pilot.

00:13:57.150 --> 00:14:02.990
This could be compared to issuing
orders to soldiers.

00:14:02.990 --> 00:14:04.530
In no operation

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:09.460
do you instruct the soldiers in each
and every action they undertake.

00:14:09.460 --> 00:14:12.570
The better trained the soldier is,

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:17.170
the better he or she will perform the
task with a minimal set of orders.

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:19.270
This is exactly like that.

00:14:19.270 --> 00:14:21.640
By putting together a system like that,

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:26.100
we've succeeded in controlling
bipedal movement.

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:31.190
We call this transmission system,
the "adaptive actuator",

00:14:31.190 --> 00:14:33.950
or adaptive artificial muscle structure.

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:43.200
Now let's observe just exactly
what the TA can do.

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:51.310
What was their reaction?

00:14:51.310 --> 00:14:54.470
I'd say, they'll believe
it when they see it.

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:58.710
But I'm sure those big shots

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:01.150
will gravitate toward supporting
the overseas deployment

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:03.840
of the TA's once they see
its abilities up front.

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:07.290
What about Yushiro?

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:11.090
I was talking to Lieutenant Colonel
Hayakawa about that.

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:16.160
As Kiyotsugu said, he probably won't
have any problems operating a TA.

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:17.220
But still...

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:47.290
First will be a movement trial.

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:52.370
Many common battlefield obstacles
have been planted in this course,

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:56.170
allowing you to observe its movement
in more realistic combat conditions.

00:15:59.210 --> 00:16:00.260
Let's begin.

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:04.730
Go!

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:18.920
It's keeping up with the tanks.

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:33.170
B!

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:46.950
Transmission efficiency 61%,
fluctuation is less than 15%.

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:49.890
Its capabilities have improved
over last time.

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:04.840
Astonishing how it went past
the tanks like that.

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:07.340
What kind of a weapon is it?

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:11.310
While it may not be necessary to point
this out, our SSDF's Type 12 tank

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:15.610
is one of the world's most
maneuverable and advanced vehicles.

00:17:23.590 --> 00:17:24.620
What?

00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:45.910
Enemy strength is four
tanks, four IFV's.

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:50.080
In this simulation, the opposing
sides have not been informed

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:52.620
of the type of weaponry nor
strength of their enemies.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:56.580
This is to recreate a realistic
combat situation as best as possible.

00:18:00.530 --> 00:18:04.550
Consequently, no blanks are
used in this exercise.

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:10.770
What if the equipment or
personnel are hit?

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:12.970
There's no need for concern.

00:18:12.970 --> 00:18:17.510
Each unit has been equipped with a
SimFire laser simulation system,

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:21.320
so if they actually do have an enemy
targeted, the weapon will not function.

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:25.850
Instead, simulated footage determines
targeting and damage.

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:29.020
Focus One, picking up a tank on
your twelve. Use your ASDIC.

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:26.910
Four tanks neutralized in
the blink of an eye.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:46.830
Damage to right leg.

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:00.840
What the hell is that?

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:09.490
Are you all right?

00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:11.230
I'm right above you now.

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:12.760
Damage to right leg.

00:20:12.760 --> 00:20:16.600
The automatic repair program has
functioned to allow you to move about,

00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:19.570
but your maneuverability is down by
15%.

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:23.070
Target Two will enter area of
engagement in twelve seconds.

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:24.540
Focus Two, maintain position.

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:27.530
Wait for Focus One's attack before
you attack the rear vehicle.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:31.110
This combat simulation is...

00:20:31.110 --> 00:20:32.450
That's right.

00:20:32.450 --> 00:20:36.880
The pattern is identical to when the
multinational forces were defeated.

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:39.720
What is it that you're implying?

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:56.800
Calmly analyzing the circumstances
of the engagement,

00:20:56.800 --> 00:21:02.010
it would seem logical to assume that
the Belgistan forces are also outfitted

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:04.670
with weapons with capabilities
similar to TA's.

00:21:20.690 --> 00:21:23.200
Our radar has the enemy
tanks captured.

00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:25.130
Forwarding composite image.

00:21:37.010 --> 00:21:39.950
These are the fighting
abilities of the TA's.

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:42.550
Setting aside outright engagement on
the open field, in limited engagements

00:21:42.550 --> 00:21:45.220
set inside bewilderingly dynamic
tactical conditions,

00:21:45.220 --> 00:21:50.250
there probably is no weapon superior
to the TA at the present time.

00:21:51.390 --> 00:21:54.290
Seems like we should go ahead
and dispatch them.

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:58.230
But how will we convince the Security
Council to accept this?

00:21:58.230 --> 00:22:00.630
It may be prudent to hold off making
an official announcement.

00:22:09.540 --> 00:22:12.880
I just got a message from Kiyotsugu.

00:22:12.880 --> 00:22:17.520
The explosion in Belgistan seemed
odd, so I had Kiyotsugu examine it.

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:21.920
He says the physical data was nearly
identical to that at the stage of stone.

00:22:23.990 --> 00:22:25.460
That means...

00:22:28.750 --> 00:22:33.710
Hark

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:40.160
It's time I journey

00:22:43.690 --> 00:22:50.830
Break apart my heart

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:57.360
For crimson sadness

00:22:57.690 --> 00:23:04.870
Pours out from it

00:23:05.080 --> 00:23:08.790
I can only, oh

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:11.980
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:12.070 --> 00:23:17.590
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:32.810 --> 00:23:36.690
I can only, oh

00:23:36.780 --> 00:23:39.840
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:39.910 --> 00:23:45.040
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:46.570 --> 00:23:53.020
I beg you, be by my side

00:23:59.990 --> 00:24:02.020
The field of battle awaits me.

00:24:02.020 --> 00:24:04.560
What that will mean to me,
I do not know.

00:24:04.560 --> 00:24:07.150
Nevertheless this is a solemn fact.

00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:13.560
I would be lying if I said I did
not feel any uneasiness.

00:24:15.170 --> 00:24:19.410
Rain and wind and all, the weather
wheel foretells the times ahead.

00:24:19.410 --> 00:24:22.200
Seeking my fate, I listen to it
spin with a lonely heart.

00:24:24.110 --> 00:24:27.270
Will I be able to see what awaits me
listening to the metal disk spin?
